  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P3] Guard against a throwing `release()` masking the work error",
      "body": "If `work()` rejects and `release()` then throws inside the `finally`, JavaScript's `finally` semantics replace the original work error with the release error, hiding the actionable failure from callers. This hazard is introduced by this PR (the old code never called `release()`), but it only bites when `release()` throws synchronously, and nothing in this repository indicates it can — so treat it as a defensive-coding improvement, e.g. swallow or log release failures in the `finally` rather than letting them propagate over the work result.",
      "severity": "P3",
